WEBVTT

00:29.154 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.909
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.579 --> 00:38.580
I found you.

00:46.672 --> 00:47.714
This is bad.

01:08.402 --> 01:10.028
Why are you…

01:11.113 --> 01:12.447
I'm just copying you.

01:14.449 --> 01:16.994
I have a habit of copying other people.

01:21.582 --> 01:24.793
-  But I can't breathe…
- Oh.

01:26.295 --> 01:27.378
Sorry.

01:29.506 --> 01:32.467
You said you hug people
you're happy to see.

01:41.852 --> 01:43.644
EPISODE 7

02:18.430 --> 02:19.890
We're here.

02:21.725 --> 02:22.726
Sir?

02:23.560 --> 02:24.603
Yes?

02:31.318 --> 02:32.818
Can you open the trunk?

02:32.819 --> 02:35.656
Just keep riding this to SHIM.
Mr. Park will be waiting.

02:49.628 --> 02:50.629
Ah.

02:51.380 --> 02:52.547
Yes, Mr. Yeon.

02:53.131 --> 02:54.382
Producer Ben?

02:54.383 --> 02:55.883
He just informed me

02:55.884 --> 02:57.969
that the collaboration project
will resume.

03:01.056 --> 03:02.182
Huh?

03:05.394 --> 03:07.978
The animation team
will return to Korea soon.

03:07.979 --> 03:10.272
All right. That's good.

03:17.447 --> 03:18.615
My roommate!

03:19.449 --> 03:21.034
Oh. Mr. Park!

03:21.576 --> 03:23.035
Mr. Park.

03:23.036 --> 03:24.829
How have you been?

03:24.830 --> 03:26.248
Sorry, I couldn't call you.

03:28.583 --> 03:29.959
You're here, so it's fine.

03:29.960 --> 03:32.336
Why are you standing out here in the cold?

03:32.337 --> 03:34.088
You didn't know when I'd get here.

03:34.089 --> 03:35.882
I just came out 10 seconds ago.

03:37.592 --> 03:39.761
Goodness. But look at you…

03:40.429 --> 03:44.056
You must have been through a lot.
You look so gaunt.

03:44.057 --> 03:45.683
Do I?

03:45.684 --> 03:47.144
That's awful.

03:47.727 --> 03:48.936
I should get prettier now.

03:50.814 --> 03:52.731
You didn't forget your meds, right?

03:52.732 --> 03:54.568
And your cardiac enzyme levels?

03:55.318 --> 03:57.069
It's cold. Let's go inside.

03:57.070 --> 04:00.322
Genius, Chan is here. Come on in.

04:00.323 --> 04:02.575
- It's cold.
- Are you running away?

04:02.576 --> 04:03.869
Mr. Park!

04:04.536 --> 04:06.871
Genius!

04:06.872 --> 04:07.997
Genius.

04:09.916 --> 04:12.961
Hey, Genius.
Aren't you going to show me your face?

04:13.545 --> 04:14.879
Hey, Grouchy.

04:14.880 --> 04:17.965
You were waiting for Chan the whole time.
Are you protesting?

04:17.966 --> 04:20.051
Leave him.

04:20.552 --> 04:22.679
He's sour because you left
without telling him.

04:23.180 --> 04:24.598
Go upstairs. You must be tired.

04:42.532 --> 04:44.868
Oh… Yes, Mr. Park. Come in.

04:48.538 --> 04:49.539
Oh?

04:51.166 --> 04:53.417
Genius.

04:53.418 --> 04:56.505
Want to sleep with me today?
Hmm?

04:58.215 --> 05:00.550
Dogs should sleep at this hour.

05:01.176 --> 05:02.177
Hmm?

05:02.677 --> 05:03.804
Me?

05:05.305 --> 05:07.474
I have a lot on my mind.

05:08.642 --> 05:13.605
Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

05:14.856 --> 05:17.734
That's all I wanted for her,

05:19.277 --> 05:20.821
but what do I do now?

05:23.114 --> 05:26.576
I want her to be happy beside me,

05:29.621 --> 05:32.165
and I want her to be happy because of me.

05:33.333 --> 05:35.043
I keep getting greedy.

05:36.211 --> 05:38.379
IF IT'S OKAY WITH YOU, YOU CAN TALK TO ME

05:38.380 --> 05:42.425
The fact that I was fake,
and the reason I became a fake…

05:43.218 --> 05:48.890
The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

05:52.727 --> 05:57.315
I keep wanting to do as I want

05:58.441 --> 05:59.860
as if I'm clueless to all that.

06:02.320 --> 06:03.989
Until I go back,

06:05.115 --> 06:08.702
if I play dumb and be greedy,

06:09.911 --> 06:11.162
would that be wrong?

06:17.168 --> 06:19.169
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

06:20.922 --> 06:22.507
Here's today's dress code.

06:22.924 --> 06:24.926
Comfy shoes and warm clothes.

06:25.719 --> 06:26.886
See you later.

06:26.887 --> 06:28.805
I can't travel too far today.

06:30.473 --> 06:31.557
CLOSED DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

06:31.558 --> 06:32.559
Oh?

06:33.727 --> 06:34.769
Hmm?

06:35.353 --> 06:37.188
Mr. Park…

06:38.273 --> 06:39.940
- Oh! Ms. Song.
- Ms. Song.

06:39.941 --> 06:41.525
- Hey.
- Hello.

06:41.526 --> 06:42.527
What are you all doing…

06:43.194 --> 06:44.778
Ben, when did you get here?

06:44.779 --> 06:45.863
Have you been well?

06:45.864 --> 06:48.407
I visited as soon as I arrived,
and now I'm trapped.

06:49.492 --> 06:51.910
We came when we saw Seunggyu's photo
in our group chat.

06:51.911 --> 06:54.788
I wanted to get the coffee
you bought us last time,

06:54.789 --> 06:57.207
and I saw that Chan was here.

06:57.208 --> 07:01.045
As soon as I saw the photo,
I rushed over with my sheet mask still on.

07:01.046 --> 07:03.464
Things worked out,
so he's staying for two months.

07:03.465 --> 07:04.840
Isn't that great?

07:04.841 --> 07:06.634
Right…

07:06.635 --> 07:07.801
Let's play.

07:07.802 --> 07:09.053
Let's play.

07:09.054 --> 07:11.680
Oh, I gave them to Genius as a gift.

07:11.681 --> 07:15.142
If he presses the buttons,
we can communicate.

07:15.143 --> 07:17.436
I have soccer class,
so I'll be back later.

07:17.437 --> 07:19.563
- Bye.
- Bye.

07:20.732 --> 07:22.358
- Bye.
-  Bye, Donggu.

07:22.359 --> 07:23.442
Bye.

07:23.443 --> 07:25.569
- See you later.
- Ms. Song, sit down.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.737
Right.

07:26.738 --> 07:30.032
We'll need some wine for a welcome party.

07:30.033 --> 07:31.950
Roomie, please get the wine glasses.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.243
Sure.

07:33.244 --> 07:36.914
Mom, I'm going home late today!

07:36.915 --> 07:40.043
Raemee, you live with your mother?
Not alone?

07:55.016 --> 07:56.142
Can I help with anything?

07:57.602 --> 07:59.062
What? Oh…

08:00.355 --> 08:02.649
Ah. It's okay. Sit down.

08:16.871 --> 08:18.414
Please let us clean up.

08:18.415 --> 08:19.623
Please.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.667
The host should clean up.

08:21.668 --> 08:24.211
Just come have some coffee next time.

08:24.212 --> 08:25.379
-  Okay.
-  All right.

08:25.380 --> 08:27.631
-  Then, we'll come have coffee.
-  Okay, thank you.

08:27.632 --> 08:29.925
Thank you.

08:29.926 --> 08:33.804
Still, shouldn't at least one of us
stay back and help clean up?

08:33.805 --> 08:36.014
We're going for another round,

08:36.015 --> 08:38.809
so you can help out here, Lightweight.

08:38.810 --> 08:40.269
- Me?
- Yes, you. Song Haran.

08:40.270 --> 08:41.687
- The lightweight.
- Ah.

08:41.688 --> 08:43.147
Then I'll stay and help too…

08:43.148 --> 08:45.149
Come on. You'll just break the cups.

08:45.150 --> 08:46.817
We'll come back next time. Bye.

08:46.818 --> 08:48.402
- See you next time.
- Okay, bye.

08:48.403 --> 08:50.071
-  I should--
-  Let's go.

08:52.115 --> 08:53.991
My gosh.

08:56.036 --> 08:59.247
I didn't expect them
to all swarm in here.

08:59.748 --> 09:00.749
Yeah.

09:04.753 --> 09:07.254
Sorry. We're going to drink this later.

09:10.216 --> 09:13.511
But it's suddenly so quiet
with all of them gone.

09:14.262 --> 09:16.556
Right. It was pretty noisy in here.

09:17.223 --> 09:18.390
But, Ms. Song--

09:18.391 --> 09:19.683
I love you.

09:25.398 --> 09:28.859
Genius, you shouldn't just
keep pressing those.

09:28.860 --> 09:30.819
What I meant to say is…

09:30.820 --> 09:31.821
I love you.

09:35.450 --> 09:38.702
Has he not been trained yet?

09:38.703 --> 09:40.622
I was trying to say

09:41.122 --> 09:44.249
that I thought you'd be startled
to see everyone here,

09:44.250 --> 09:46.752
so I sent you a message.

09:46.753 --> 09:49.838
Oh. I see.

09:49.839 --> 09:52.508
I'm so full.

09:52.509 --> 09:54.802
I'm going to take a walk with Genius.

09:54.803 --> 09:56.512
You can clean up the rest, right?

09:56.513 --> 09:57.971
Sure. Ms. Song and I--

09:57.972 --> 10:00.015
I love you.

10:00.016 --> 10:01.683
Oops.

10:01.684 --> 10:02.976
My mistake.

10:04.145 --> 10:05.688
See you later. Let's go.

10:10.485 --> 10:13.071
Let's clean this up, then.

10:16.241 --> 10:17.658
You got it on your sleeve.

10:17.659 --> 10:19.994
It'll get stained
if you don't wash it off.

10:28.336 --> 10:29.879
I'll go get changed.

10:35.760 --> 10:38.262
Training on the weekend?

10:38.263 --> 10:39.848
I'm wasting my youth.

10:41.474 --> 10:43.183
Oh? It's Song Hadam.

10:43.184 --> 10:44.727
Oh? It's Cha Yougyum.

10:50.817 --> 10:52.067
Hi.

10:52.068 --> 10:53.569
I'm Kim Seokhyeon from Class 1.

10:53.570 --> 10:55.571
I've been interested in you,

10:55.572 --> 10:57.991
but I don't have to give up
because of Yougyum now.

10:59.075 --> 11:00.367
Can I have your number?

11:00.368 --> 11:02.287
Hey, what is he saying?

11:02.871 --> 11:04.497
Did you two break up?

11:04.998 --> 11:07.624
Cha Yougyum,
are you just going to watch?

11:07.625 --> 11:10.836
If you don't come until I count to three,
I'm giving him my number.

11:10.837 --> 11:13.548
One, two…

11:17.177 --> 11:18.720
All right. I'll give it to you.

11:23.433 --> 11:24.642
Text me.

11:31.107 --> 11:33.066
You got her number.

11:33.067 --> 11:35.485
-  What's this?
-  What?

11:35.486 --> 11:38.322
Please call me if you see her.

11:38.323 --> 11:41.617
If you ever see my mother,
please give me a call.

11:41.618 --> 11:43.077
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

11:46.664 --> 11:47.916
Kim Nabong.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.501
Hey, Manjae.

11:51.377 --> 11:52.669
Park Genius.

11:52.670 --> 11:55.589
Genius, how have you been?

11:55.590 --> 11:57.174
Were you taking a walk?

11:57.175 --> 11:59.384
Yes, this is a good place to work out.

11:59.385 --> 12:01.803
- I walk a few laps every day.
- No way.

12:01.804 --> 12:04.056
I walk him every day here, too.

12:04.057 --> 12:07.726
Well, I guess we wouldn't have
recognized each other until now.

12:08.811 --> 12:11.230
We can be walking buddies from now on.

12:12.398 --> 12:13.565
Hey.

12:13.566 --> 12:15.108
I think he needs to poop.

12:15.109 --> 12:17.319
He has his own poop area over there.

12:17.320 --> 12:18.862
- Gosh.
- Go and let him poop.

12:18.863 --> 12:21.073
Okay, I'll see you later.

12:21.074 --> 12:23.075
Hey, Genius! Slow down.

12:23.076 --> 12:24.826
All right. Goodness.

12:24.827 --> 12:26.746
Slow down. Okay.

12:33.044 --> 12:35.963
What was she doing here?

12:35.964 --> 12:39.092
- Are you sick or anything?
- I was just visiting a friend there.

12:45.223 --> 12:47.141
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

12:57.318 --> 12:58.736
Is that you, Yougyum?

13:02.907 --> 13:03.992
Hello.

13:05.118 --> 13:06.952
Why are you wearing glasses?

13:06.953 --> 13:08.704
I almost didn't recognize you.

13:08.705 --> 13:10.414
My eyes are swollen.

13:10.415 --> 13:11.666
How swollen can they be?

13:12.333 --> 13:16.086
My goodness.
They really are incredibly puffy.

13:16.087 --> 13:17.880
How did your eyes get like…

13:19.132 --> 13:20.466
Are you crying?

13:22.677 --> 13:25.304
I had a fight with Hadam,

13:25.305 --> 13:27.724
and it feels like
my whole world just fell apart.

13:29.851 --> 13:33.187
How do I live from now on, Ms. Kim?

13:35.481 --> 13:36.482
Follow me.

13:37.525 --> 13:39.444
What? Where…

13:43.823 --> 13:47.325
Fighting won't make the world fall apart.
It only exhausts you.

13:47.326 --> 13:48.369
Eat up.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.579
I don't have an appetite.

13:50.580 --> 13:54.500
To me, Hadam is my whole world
and my whole universe…

13:55.334 --> 13:57.587
You're out. Just break up with Hadam.

13:58.171 --> 13:59.713
- What?
- I'm not letting a guy

13:59.714 --> 14:02.507
who bawls after one fight
about the world falling apart

14:02.508 --> 14:03.842
date my granddaughter.

14:03.843 --> 14:06.261
How will you survive the big leagues
with that mentality?

14:06.262 --> 14:07.889
You're out.

14:08.473 --> 14:09.766
No…

14:10.516 --> 14:11.684
I'll eat.

14:13.519 --> 14:14.896
Too hot!

14:15.772 --> 14:19.357
I'm only weak when it comes to Hadam.
I push myself hard when I'm training.

14:19.358 --> 14:21.319
I'm the ruthless Cha Yougyum.

14:24.322 --> 14:28.451
Right. At your age, you think the world
falls apart with the smallest things.

14:29.577 --> 14:30.703
I did, too.

14:32.622 --> 14:36.666
But once you go through
something really serious,

14:36.667 --> 14:40.962
you'll realize
that the issues you thought were huge

14:40.963 --> 14:43.215
were actually just tiny specks.

14:43.216 --> 14:47.385
And you'll regret not facing
those issues head-on back then.

14:47.386 --> 14:49.639
You'll think, "Why was I such a coward?"

14:50.765 --> 14:54.392
Anyway, there are dozens of more serious
problems waiting for you in life.

14:54.393 --> 14:55.895
So stop being weak.

14:56.979 --> 14:58.106
Okay.

14:59.357 --> 15:02.693
I'm sorry.
I was absorbed in my own issues.

15:03.402 --> 15:04.945
Ah. What about your checkup?

15:04.946 --> 15:08.365
Something came up at work,
so I rescheduled.

15:08.366 --> 15:10.784
I got scolded
for disappearing from the hospital.

15:17.708 --> 15:20.878
I learned that abalones contain ta…

15:21.712 --> 15:22.963
Ta…

15:22.964 --> 15:24.131
Taurine.

15:24.132 --> 15:26.884
They contain taurine,
which helps with cognitive function.

15:28.970 --> 15:31.389
All right. Give me all the abalones.

15:32.557 --> 15:35.225
I still have a lot to do,
so I have to stay strong.

15:35.226 --> 15:38.687
You eat up, too.
You need the energy to make up with Hadam.

15:38.688 --> 15:40.188
Right. Energy.

15:42.775 --> 15:45.068
Gosh, that's hot.

15:59.917 --> 16:01.501
Mr. Seonu.

16:04.755 --> 16:07.633
Mr. Seonu, there's someone calling you.

16:11.429 --> 16:14.557
Someone keeps calling…

16:15.766 --> 16:16.934
Is he not here?

16:18.769 --> 16:20.438
I'm sorry.

16:21.272 --> 16:22.315
Right.

16:23.065 --> 16:25.317
What is it?

16:25.318 --> 16:26.610
I…

16:28.070 --> 16:30.865
Someone kept calling,
so it seemed important.

16:31.616 --> 16:33.950
- I'm sorry.
- Wait.

16:33.951 --> 16:35.493
Yes?

16:35.494 --> 16:36.495
I mean…

16:46.631 --> 16:50.218
We shouldn't do it here…

16:50.801 --> 16:52.053
- I mean…
- No, I…

16:56.098 --> 16:58.476
- Why are you turning off the lights?
- You…

17:06.901 --> 17:08.778
You're the one who turned them off.

17:11.405 --> 17:12.615
With your back.

17:15.159 --> 17:17.494
Oh. My back…

17:17.495 --> 17:19.037
You've got something on your lips.

17:19.038 --> 17:21.706
Crumbs or something.

17:21.707 --> 17:23.960
It was the crackers…

17:26.045 --> 17:28.296
But why did you close your eyes?

17:31.133 --> 17:34.803
Honestly, anyone would have
misunderstood that situation.

17:34.804 --> 17:38.265
You held my hand and hugged me yesterday,
so I thought…

17:38.266 --> 17:39.392
You thought what?

17:40.476 --> 17:43.938
I just thought you were moving fast
since you're from the States.

17:44.438 --> 17:46.315
This is getting weird.

17:46.816 --> 17:48.525
Stop teasing me.

17:48.526 --> 17:49.818
I wasn't teasing you.

17:49.819 --> 17:52.154
I just thought I saw the old you.

17:52.863 --> 17:54.197
It was cute.

17:54.198 --> 17:55.657
My old self?

17:55.658 --> 17:57.493
What do you mean?

18:00.246 --> 18:02.582
I think I heard you used to be
much more cheerful.

18:03.374 --> 18:04.375
From who?

18:05.293 --> 18:06.544
Was it Hayeong?

18:07.336 --> 18:10.464
Anyway,
I really wasn't teasing you.

18:10.965 --> 18:12.883
I'm sorry.

18:15.136 --> 18:17.805
Ah. I forgot to give you this.

18:18.973 --> 18:20.141
A welcome drink.

18:21.851 --> 18:24.145
I almost took back my word
about being nice to you.

18:26.689 --> 18:28.232
Can we do it now?

18:28.983 --> 18:29.984
Do what?

18:30.901 --> 18:32.777
I meant…

18:32.778 --> 18:34.696
The photos.

18:34.697 --> 18:35.990
Let's check your homework.

18:46.751 --> 18:49.545
You have a talent for this.

18:50.171 --> 18:52.298
Oh, my gosh.

18:55.134 --> 18:57.386
You liar.
You said there were just 10 shots.

18:59.889 --> 19:03.308
Hmm? My Destinations List…

19:03.309 --> 19:06.062
It's yours. I took a photo of it.

19:07.063 --> 19:09.565
- When did you take this?
- What?

19:10.107 --> 19:11.316
This!

19:11.317 --> 19:15.820
I just took this for fun
when I was bored…

19:15.821 --> 19:17.823
Wow. That's not fair.

19:18.491 --> 19:20.034
You promised to do that with me.

19:21.035 --> 19:22.786
That doesn't count. I'm confiscating this.

19:22.787 --> 19:24.621
Everything you did alone is invalid.

19:24.622 --> 19:26.665
We'll do everything together.

19:26.666 --> 19:28.584
Geez.

19:30.044 --> 19:33.755
But what's that last thing
you scribbled out?

19:33.756 --> 19:36.634
Mmm.

19:37.301 --> 19:40.763
I thought it would be impossible,
so I scribbled it out…

19:44.892 --> 19:46.227
but it might be possible now.

19:47.812 --> 19:49.146
It's a secret, though.

19:52.650 --> 19:55.193
Why did you tell me
to wear comfy shoes today?

19:55.194 --> 19:58.571
I thought we'd just walk around a bit

19:58.572 --> 20:00.448
without any specific plans.

20:00.449 --> 20:02.283
Just go wherever the wind takes us?

20:03.661 --> 20:05.871
I wanted to try that with you.

20:06.497 --> 20:08.039
Go somewhere and try things

20:08.040 --> 20:11.335
without thinking of what happens next.

20:12.503 --> 20:13.546
No,

20:14.505 --> 20:16.632
that may have messed things up.

20:17.425 --> 20:21.095
If things get messed up, we can fix them.
It's the same for knots.

20:21.929 --> 20:24.807
Sometimes they seem impossible to undo,

20:25.307 --> 20:28.602
but if you loosen one strand at a time,
they'll unravel.

20:29.937 --> 20:32.857
You can find a way,
no matter how impossible it seems.

20:35.943 --> 20:37.445
Shall we do it tomorrow?

20:38.195 --> 20:40.990
Try going wherever the wind takes us.

20:41.782 --> 20:43.283
Sorry. Next time.

20:43.284 --> 20:46.453
I have to go somewhere far
with my family tomorrow.

20:46.454 --> 20:47.913
Far? Where?

20:51.459 --> 20:52.460
Ah.

20:53.377 --> 20:54.794
THE LATE SONG JUNHO
THE LATE MIN HYEWON

20:54.795 --> 20:58.090
Dad's favorite crab stew.

21:00.509 --> 21:03.803
Remember when Dad chipped his tooth
eating crab stew?

21:03.804 --> 21:06.724
Right, he visited the dentist
for a long time after that.

21:08.100 --> 21:09.768
Hadam, wait.

21:09.769 --> 21:12.480
Put the castella on Mom's favorite dish.

21:13.272 --> 21:16.941
Wow. That's a real antique.
We've had that since I was a baby.

21:16.942 --> 21:19.819
Whenever we were in a bad mood,
she gave us snacks on this.

21:19.820 --> 21:21.571
Mom always said,

21:21.572 --> 21:25.533
"When you're feeling down,
having sweets on a pretty dish

21:25.534 --> 21:27.786
- will make you feel sparkly."
- Sparkly.

21:35.044 --> 21:36.712
-  Let's greet them now.
-  Okay.

21:41.342 --> 21:45.054
This might be
my last time coming here.

21:46.680 --> 21:47.972
If, by any chance,

21:47.973 --> 21:51.268
I start acting too strange,
just call me home to you quickly.

21:51.852 --> 21:54.855
I don't want to embarrass myself
in front of them.

21:55.523 --> 21:56.649
Okay, Hyewon?

21:57.566 --> 21:58.776
Okay, Junho?

22:06.784 --> 22:09.786
I will take you all home safely.

22:09.787 --> 22:10.996
Let's go.

22:13.791 --> 22:18.711
Ah…
My bad feelings are never wrong.

22:18.712 --> 22:19.713
I forgot my phone.

22:21.257 --> 22:23.633
- I'm riding with Haran.
- Eh?

22:23.634 --> 22:26.345
You're really going to betray me? Hey!

22:28.889 --> 22:30.641
She's so cold.

22:31.851 --> 22:34.395
♪ I dream a little bit of red alone ♪

22:41.193 --> 22:42.694
No, I had it then.

22:42.695 --> 22:43.987
And then, Grandma…

22:43.988 --> 22:47.283
I greeted Mom and Dad,
then I got up, and my phone…

22:47.741 --> 22:49.243
Where did I leave it?

22:50.744 --> 22:51.911
-  I'm really sorry.
- Eh?

22:51.912 --> 22:52.996
Who's that?

22:52.997 --> 22:54.247
I'm sorry.

22:54.248 --> 22:56.916
Excuse me, that's my parents' grave.

22:56.917 --> 22:58.711
I think you came to the wrong…

23:00.754 --> 23:01.964
Mr. Yeon?

23:02.590 --> 23:03.883
Why are you…

23:05.009 --> 23:06.092
Are you crying?

23:06.093 --> 23:08.219
Oh… No.

23:08.220 --> 23:10.639
You are. Your eyes are red.

23:11.181 --> 23:13.267
People would think
you're their son…

23:17.563 --> 23:18.689
Thank you.

23:19.773 --> 23:21.399
How pretty.

23:21.400 --> 23:24.110
You don't need to do this
for Parents' Day.

23:24.111 --> 23:27.322
You always welcome me
and pack me side dishes.

23:27.323 --> 23:30.325
I'm a bit awkward
with expressing my feelings,

23:30.326 --> 23:32.785
but I really wanted to thank you today.

23:34.288 --> 23:35.872
Goodness. Thank you.

23:35.873 --> 23:37.790
My friends brag about their sons.

23:37.791 --> 23:40.585
I can brag to them that I got
carnations from my son, too.

23:41.712 --> 23:45.256
Since we're all dressed up,
how about a family photo?

23:45.257 --> 23:46.799
That sounds great.

23:46.800 --> 23:48.676
- Let's take a photo over there.
- Okay.

23:48.677 --> 23:51.679
- Oh, sure.
-  Let's take a photo.

23:51.680 --> 23:53.681
- All right.
-  Mr. Yeon.

23:53.682 --> 23:55.975
- Let's take it together.
- Come on, Mr. Yeon.

23:55.976 --> 23:57.602
- Join us.
- Come here.

23:57.603 --> 23:59.103
It's okay.

23:59.104 --> 24:01.105
It's a family photo. Come here.

24:01.106 --> 24:03.943
Sir, can you take a photo of us?

24:05.486 --> 24:06.694
All right.

24:06.695 --> 24:08.279
One, two, three.

24:18.248 --> 24:19.791
Mom, Dad.

24:19.792 --> 24:22.794
Our former chauffeur, Mr. Yeon,
became our COO.

24:22.795 --> 24:26.924
He's a core figure now,
like me in our household.

24:27.508 --> 24:30.052
So send him lots of energy.

24:33.973 --> 24:35.683
Thank you for taking care

24:36.934 --> 24:38.477
of our parents, too.

24:41.438 --> 24:42.439
I'm sorry.

24:42.898 --> 24:45.608
Why do you keep saying sorry?

24:45.609 --> 24:46.610
I…

24:48.404 --> 24:50.030
I'm really sorry.

24:53.575 --> 24:56.744
Oh. I dropped my phone somewhere.

24:56.745 --> 24:58.205
Can you call my number?

25:01.834 --> 25:04.002
Where is it?

25:04.003 --> 25:05.921
I hear it. Where is it?

25:07.131 --> 25:08.966
Is it here? Is it here?

25:09.550 --> 25:10.633
Is it here?

25:10.634 --> 25:11.635
I…

25:12.803 --> 25:14.304
It's coming from your butt.

25:15.014 --> 25:16.849
My butt?

25:17.474 --> 25:21.020
Darn it. I came all the way
back up here for nothing.

25:21.770 --> 25:24.773
Since we met here,

25:25.566 --> 25:26.817
should we go eat something?

25:27.234 --> 25:28.317
Eat?

25:28.318 --> 25:30.570
I promised you I'd treat you last time.

25:30.571 --> 25:34.116
It was 39,000 won last time,

25:35.701 --> 25:38.494
so I'll treat you to up to 80,000 won.

25:38.495 --> 25:41.539
There's an amazing
oxtail soup place nearby.

25:41.540 --> 25:42.623
What do you say?

25:42.624 --> 25:43.875
Let's go!

25:43.876 --> 25:45.835
It's okay…

25:45.836 --> 25:47.379
No, it's not okay.

25:48.005 --> 25:49.922
Have we eaten together before?

25:49.923 --> 25:52.050
Who do you normally
have lunch with at work?

25:52.051 --> 25:54.677
What do you usually do on the weekend?

25:54.678 --> 25:55.845
Wait.

26:00.142 --> 26:01.225
Your hand.

26:01.226 --> 26:03.353
You might slip
since you're wearing heels.

26:07.483 --> 26:08.942
It's fine, I can wipe them.

26:09.610 --> 26:10.611
Be careful.

26:19.203 --> 26:21.538
You really are considerate.

26:22.247 --> 26:24.500
You always look out for our family.

26:27.961 --> 26:29.922
Why did he cry, though?

26:37.346 --> 26:38.972
How was your visit to your parents?

26:39.473 --> 26:40.807
Hey.

26:40.808 --> 26:43.227
Whose message
is making you smile like that?

26:43.852 --> 26:45.228
What?

26:45.229 --> 26:48.022
What took you so long?
Weren't you looking for your phone?

26:48.023 --> 26:49.942
I was hungry, so I got some oxtail soup.

26:50.567 --> 26:52.193
I'm so full.

26:52.194 --> 26:53.569
That's good.

26:53.570 --> 26:54.947
Hey, Hayeong.

26:55.739 --> 26:59.992
Did you ever tell Mr. Seonu about my past?

26:59.993 --> 27:03.037
Like how I was different before
or something like that?

27:03.038 --> 27:06.541
Like how you used to be
really bubbly and friendly?

27:06.542 --> 27:08.000
Something like that.

27:08.001 --> 27:09.545
Mmm? No, I didn't…

27:11.004 --> 27:12.881
Wait, did I?

27:13.715 --> 27:16.050
I'm 29 now.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.261
My memory isn't so good…

27:18.595 --> 27:21.849
- But why do you ask?
- He spoke as if he knew me.

27:22.307 --> 27:23.308
Really?

27:24.476 --> 27:27.603
But are you two really close?

27:27.604 --> 27:29.814
Mr. Seonu, Ms. Song…

27:29.815 --> 27:30.941
You're so formal.

27:31.775 --> 27:33.818
Then what should I call him?

27:33.819 --> 27:35.486
You're the same age.

27:35.487 --> 27:37.196
Use your first names.

27:37.197 --> 27:39.867
You can just say, "Hey, Haran. Hey, Chan…"

27:42.452 --> 27:43.703
I should go shower.

27:43.704 --> 27:45.080
Why did you suddenly stop?

27:45.914 --> 27:46.999
Well…

27:48.125 --> 27:50.335
You used to call him Chan.

27:51.128 --> 27:54.423
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

27:55.716 --> 27:57.885
I just realized their names were similar.

27:58.760 --> 28:00.219
Oh…

28:00.220 --> 28:02.847
Right. I didn't think about that.

28:07.352 --> 28:09.145
Make…

28:09.146 --> 28:12.774
MAKE HER HAPPY AGAIN, NO MATTER WHAT!

28:14.776 --> 28:17.446
Their names… were similar.

28:18.238 --> 28:19.489
All right…

28:28.832 --> 28:30.292
What was that?

28:30.792 --> 28:33.670
EMPTY SPOT IN MEMORY - FOURTH

28:34.838 --> 28:37.007
A waste container…

28:37.883 --> 28:38.967
and that sound again.

28:41.011 --> 28:42.511
The lab…

28:42.512 --> 28:44.096
The sound of metal…

28:44.097 --> 28:45.431
The explosion.

28:45.432 --> 28:49.102
The missing gap
started with that sound, too.

28:52.773 --> 28:54.608
And the second memory

28:55.233 --> 28:56.443
had that sound as well.

28:59.821 --> 29:03.784
And the third memory
had the same sound.

29:05.243 --> 29:07.079
Why did those missing memories

29:07.871 --> 29:10.122
start with the sound of her bracelet?

29:10.123 --> 29:12.124
Sorry, Ran.
My professor's calling.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.292
I'll call you back later.

29:13.293 --> 29:14.628
Hey, Sujin. You're here?

29:15.128 --> 29:18.799
Why are they all connected to this person?

29:22.469 --> 29:25.263
SUJIN?

29:26.181 --> 29:27.724
Sujin?

29:44.658 --> 29:46.325
This is Cha Sujin.

29:46.326 --> 29:47.994
I've arrived in Korea.

29:47.995 --> 29:49.997
I'll head to the hospital straight away.

29:56.795 --> 29:59.047
It's my fault for causing
the misunderstanding.

29:59.756 --> 30:00.924
I'm sorry.

30:02.342 --> 30:03.760
I'm sorry about everything.

30:09.266 --> 30:10.767
I'm sorry about everything.

30:11.393 --> 30:12.769
I'm sorry about everything…

30:19.026 --> 30:21.319
I'll give it to you. Text me.

30:45.052 --> 30:46.053
Cha Yougyum?

30:47.971 --> 30:50.139
Hey, what are you doing here?

31:09.743 --> 31:11.495
What are you doing? Give it.

31:26.343 --> 31:27.552
Are you okay?

31:28.386 --> 31:29.762
Oh?

31:29.763 --> 31:30.846
That's Mom's dish.

31:30.847 --> 31:32.431
Song Hadam.

31:32.432 --> 31:34.016
Don't you know we never use that?

31:34.017 --> 31:35.893
There are dozens of dishes. Why did you--

31:35.894 --> 31:38.395
Then why are you making a fuss
over one dish?

31:38.396 --> 31:40.981
Hey. Why are you talking like that?

31:40.982 --> 31:42.942
Don't you know what that dish is?

31:42.943 --> 31:44.152
- It's Mom's--
- I don't!

31:44.903 --> 31:46.028
I don't know.

31:46.029 --> 31:47.822
I'm the only one who doesn't know.

31:47.823 --> 31:50.533
I can hardly even remember
Mom and Dad's voices or faces,

31:50.534 --> 31:53.369
so how would I know
how special that stupid dish is?

31:53.370 --> 31:55.621
I want to remember, too.

31:55.622 --> 31:57.582
I want to miss them too,

31:58.250 --> 32:00.335
but I can't remember.

32:02.379 --> 32:07.175
Whenever you talk about Mom and Dad,
I feel like I don't belong.

32:08.009 --> 32:10.762
I feel like I'm the only one
who wasn't their daughter.

32:12.264 --> 32:14.891
- Hey…
- I was only six.

32:15.517 --> 32:16.726
I…

32:18.019 --> 32:19.562
I didn't know anything…

32:21.148 --> 32:22.149
Hadam.

32:22.858 --> 32:23.983
We're sorry.

32:23.984 --> 32:25.569
I'm sorry, Hadam.

32:30.615 --> 32:31.825
I'm going to school.

32:32.742 --> 32:34.119
I'm really sorry…

32:36.788 --> 32:37.998
I broke Mom's dish.

32:49.801 --> 32:53.221
You said you have a meeting.
Go get ready. I'll clean this.

32:55.724 --> 32:56.808
Okay, thanks.

32:57.434 --> 32:59.436
We'll talk to Hadam when she comes home.

33:11.239 --> 33:12.365
Hey, Hadam.

33:15.535 --> 33:17.579
Let me see your hand. Where is it?

33:18.580 --> 33:19.831
Gosh.

33:25.962 --> 33:28.172
I just got this at a convenience store.

33:28.173 --> 33:29.548
It's just a temporary fix,

33:29.549 --> 33:32.886
so go to the nurse's office, okay?

33:34.012 --> 33:36.473
But what do we do

33:37.474 --> 33:38.683
about Mom's dish?

33:39.267 --> 33:41.101
That dish isn't the problem.

33:41.102 --> 33:43.104
You hurt your hand
when the CSAT is coming up.

33:43.772 --> 33:45.398
I'm ambidextrous.

33:46.650 --> 33:48.734
You are? Since when?

33:48.735 --> 33:50.611
I practiced using my left hand

33:50.612 --> 33:52.738
because my hand hurt
when I studied too long.

33:52.739 --> 33:54.282
But I was a natural at it.

33:54.950 --> 33:56.201
Our baby sister.

33:56.952 --> 33:58.245
You take after Mom.

33:59.871 --> 34:00.872
Mom?

34:01.957 --> 34:03.541
Mom was ambidextrous.

34:04.417 --> 34:06.543
We wondered
where her genes went.

34:06.544 --> 34:08.463
I guess they all went to you.

34:10.882 --> 34:14.886
Did you want to find out
what she meant by feeling sparkly?

34:15.887 --> 34:17.180
Is that why you took it out?

34:17.806 --> 34:18.889
Huh?

34:18.890 --> 34:23.436
Didn't you want to eat sweets from it
and feel better?

34:27.315 --> 34:28.524
Hadam.

34:28.525 --> 34:31.236
Let's talk more about Mom and Dad
from now on.

34:32.445 --> 34:37.116
I was actually worried
we'd forget about them when time passed.

34:37.117 --> 34:40.786
But I guess we can tell
our smart baby sister about them

34:40.787 --> 34:42.205
as a backup file.

34:43.373 --> 34:46.375
I do have a good memory.

34:47.752 --> 34:51.089
How long are you going to follow me?

34:52.549 --> 34:55.760
I'm escorting you properly today,

34:56.219 --> 34:57.387
all the way to school.

34:58.513 --> 35:03.101
Aren't you the least bit aware
of your current condition?

35:04.311 --> 35:06.813
- Are you embarrassed of me?
- A bit.

35:07.606 --> 35:08.856
Hadam!

35:08.857 --> 35:10.441
Oh? It's Yeongju.

35:10.442 --> 35:11.734
Bye.

35:11.735 --> 35:12.861
Jeong Yeongju!

35:13.653 --> 35:15.322
Go to the nurse's office!

35:16.406 --> 35:18.825
You'll catch a cold. Go home.

35:19.909 --> 35:21.536
Bye!

35:34.424 --> 35:36.843
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

35:39.346 --> 35:42.264
Let's go on a walk.

35:42.265 --> 35:44.433
-  Genius.
-  Let's go on a walk.

35:44.434 --> 35:46.393
You seem to be abusing that.

35:46.394 --> 35:50.689
And you're such a chatterbox.

35:50.690 --> 35:51.900
Watch your mouth, okay?

35:53.360 --> 35:55.945
-  Let's play.
- Okay.

35:56.571 --> 35:57.655
Let's go on a walk.

35:57.656 --> 35:59.865
Mr. Park, I'll go on a run with Genius.

35:59.866 --> 36:01.325
Don't you have a meeting?

36:01.326 --> 36:02.743
I still have some time.

36:02.744 --> 36:04.036
Right.

36:04.037 --> 36:07.331
Something arrived from the US
while you were away.

36:07.332 --> 36:10.042
I forgot about it.
It's in the counter cabinet.

36:10.043 --> 36:11.044
Ah.

36:27.936 --> 36:28.937
Mmm?

36:33.525 --> 36:34.526
Hello?

36:35.985 --> 36:37.487
What was that message?

36:38.071 --> 36:39.656
Why is it a secret from Ms. Song?

36:42.325 --> 36:43.326
Ah.

36:44.035 --> 36:46.538
Okay, I'll keep it a secret. All right.

36:48.915 --> 36:50.541
What did you receive?

36:50.542 --> 36:53.293
It's nothing special.

36:55.547 --> 36:57.798
I'll clean up. Go. He's so eager to leave.

36:59.175 --> 37:01.010
- Genius, let's go. Come on.
- Go on.

37:01.886 --> 37:03.846
Let's go, Genius.

37:03.847 --> 37:05.056
Let's run!

37:15.650 --> 37:16.651
What is this?

37:17.235 --> 37:20.155
"Newbury Street, Boston…"

37:20.989 --> 37:22.615
What was the package?

37:23.658 --> 37:25.075
-  Hello, Mr. Park.
- Oh!

37:25.076 --> 37:27.203
-  Hello.
- Welcome. Come in.

37:32.083 --> 37:34.835
You mean there will be
more parts on Korea?

37:34.836 --> 37:38.464
Yes, the interim feedback
was really positive.

37:38.465 --> 37:41.300
The response to Won's outfit
was incredible.

37:41.301 --> 37:45.971
The cloud motif, Korean color palette,
dancheong, and the hanbok panel.

37:45.972 --> 37:51.143
Wow. Everyone was impressed
by the details that represented Korea.

37:51.144 --> 37:56.149
The most Korean things
are what end up being popular worldwide!

37:56.733 --> 38:01.279
So we'd like to request another outfit
once we get the revised script,

38:02.113 --> 38:04.364
if that's okay with you…

38:04.365 --> 38:07.035
Don't be silly. Of course, that's okay.

38:07.827 --> 38:10.205
If it will help with the project,
anything's fine.

38:12.165 --> 38:13.583
- Thank you.
-  Thank you.

38:14.125 --> 38:16.460
Right. We just have to push
straight ahead now.

38:16.461 --> 38:18.587
Let's pick up the pace again.

38:18.588 --> 38:20.422
How about a round of applause?

38:20.423 --> 38:22.925
Everybody, clap!

38:32.519 --> 38:35.188
Plans? Is it about work?

38:36.105 --> 38:37.272
Mmm…

38:37.273 --> 38:39.108
I think it's a secret.

38:46.407 --> 38:49.244
There should at least be
one pen that you like.

38:51.329 --> 38:53.498
I guess she didn't find
any that she liked.

38:53.998 --> 38:55.082
What?

38:55.083 --> 38:56.208
It's nothing.

38:57.502 --> 38:58.878
Bye, then.

39:00.380 --> 39:01.506
Bye.

39:03.091 --> 39:04.551
See you later. I'll text you.

39:09.347 --> 39:11.891
Who is he meeting, though?

39:12.684 --> 39:15.602
Then are your parents
in LA as well?

39:16.896 --> 39:19.440
Oh… No.

39:19.983 --> 39:22.234
My mother passed away when I was nine.

39:22.235 --> 39:26.280
My father's probably teaching in Daejeon.

39:26.281 --> 39:27.824
We don't really keep in touch.

39:28.867 --> 39:29.868
Well…

39:30.368 --> 39:34.664
Every family has its own issues.

39:35.540 --> 39:37.207
Go on and eat.

39:37.208 --> 39:38.667
Thank you.

39:38.668 --> 39:39.918
Right.

39:39.919 --> 39:43.088
Will you stay in LA again
once the collaboration is over?

39:44.257 --> 39:47.010
Yes, I believe so. But why do you ask?

39:48.094 --> 39:50.555
Should I establish a branch in LA
and send her there?

39:51.598 --> 39:52.848
Excuse me?

39:52.849 --> 39:55.475
Ah. I was just talking to myself.

39:55.476 --> 39:59.187
But why aren't you eating? Hmm?

39:59.188 --> 40:02.691
I wanted to treat you to something
after all that trouble at headquarters.

40:02.692 --> 40:03.817
Eat up.

40:03.818 --> 40:07.779
Why did you only ask for me?
Ben went through a lot, too.

40:07.780 --> 40:09.782
- Who?
- You know, with the…

40:10.366 --> 40:13.619
Oh… Producer Ben?

40:13.620 --> 40:15.037
Well,

40:15.038 --> 40:18.206
I'm sure his in-laws
will take good care of him.

40:18.207 --> 40:21.501
Just think of this as a meal
from your in-laws.

40:21.502 --> 40:23.796
In-laws?

40:24.672 --> 40:28.008
I'm just saying…

40:28.009 --> 40:30.053
Darn it. I can't do this.

40:32.055 --> 40:33.347
I'm sorry.

40:33.348 --> 40:35.933
Beating around the bush
isn't really my style,

40:35.934 --> 40:37.517
so let me be blunt.

40:37.518 --> 40:39.228
Oh. Sure, be blunt…

40:39.854 --> 40:41.731
I mean, feel free to say what you want.

40:43.441 --> 40:46.486
How much do you know about Haran's past?

40:47.487 --> 40:48.780
Quite a lot.

40:50.239 --> 40:52.700
Did you hear about her losing her parents?

40:54.243 --> 40:55.327
I heard.

40:55.328 --> 40:58.539
And losing her boyfriend seven years ago?

41:01.960 --> 41:03.336
I know that, too.

41:06.673 --> 41:08.049
Even after losing her parents,

41:09.050 --> 41:11.469
she stayed strong,

41:12.387 --> 41:15.556
but that incident left Haran
trapped in winter,

41:16.432 --> 41:18.643
just like you said.

41:20.520 --> 41:22.062
Haran's not eating.

41:22.063 --> 41:23.480
Again?

41:23.481 --> 41:26.817
She's not eating or sleeping.

41:26.818 --> 41:28.319
She'll die at this rate, Grandma.

41:29.779 --> 41:32.698
She no longer smiled
or showed any expressions…

41:32.699 --> 41:35.492
- Eat a sausage, Hadam.
- …even in front of her sisters,

41:35.493 --> 41:37.995
and even in front of me,
when we used to be like friends.

41:37.996 --> 41:39.788
Just don't go.

41:39.789 --> 41:42.249
What if something happens to you outside?

41:42.250 --> 41:45.294
It happened to Mom and Dad.
So don't go, okay?

41:46.212 --> 41:49.589
It's okay.
Haran, it's all right. It's okay.

41:49.590 --> 41:52.010
If I let her stay buried
in all that anxiety,

41:52.593 --> 41:54.262
I felt like I would lose her.

41:59.142 --> 42:00.350
Come out.

42:00.351 --> 42:01.352
I'm not eating.

42:02.437 --> 42:03.895
Just leave me alone.

42:03.896 --> 42:05.564
Get up. Right now.

42:05.565 --> 42:09.569
I knew I had to do whatever I could
to pull her out.

42:10.570 --> 42:12.195
You're working here from now on.

42:12.196 --> 42:14.364
I'll give you a month
to organize the storage room.

42:14.365 --> 42:16.451
Why are you doing this?

42:17.160 --> 42:19.162
I don't want to. I'm leaving.

42:19.787 --> 42:20.871
That's an order.

42:20.872 --> 42:23.249
If you want to keep sleeping
under my roof,

42:23.875 --> 42:25.001
do as I say.

42:25.835 --> 42:29.379
I had to grow cold,
and I had to stay strong.

42:29.380 --> 42:32.759
I had to save her first.

43:12.256 --> 43:13.549
Come out.

43:18.763 --> 43:21.139
She could hardly move an inch,

43:21.140 --> 43:24.518
but she finally started moving
little by little,

43:24.519 --> 43:26.187
and her eyes started shining.

43:37.448 --> 43:40.535
She was living again,
little by little.

43:50.044 --> 43:51.587
She's alive now.

44:02.598 --> 44:04.851
Come to work on the third floor
starting tomorrow.

44:05.685 --> 44:10.398
You'll be the rookie assistant
for Design Team 1, 2, and 3.

44:12.817 --> 44:16.153
I was relieved at the fact
that she held on once more

44:16.154 --> 44:18.029
without crumbling down.

44:18.030 --> 44:20.740
But then, she changed.

44:20.741 --> 44:23.618
- This is an apology for taking a leave.
-  Thank you.

44:23.619 --> 44:25.538
She started smiling again recently.

44:26.622 --> 44:29.499
I know I met a great person.

44:29.500 --> 44:31.252
I feel grateful.

44:32.253 --> 44:33.880
She learned how to cry again, too.

44:38.634 --> 44:39.760
Mr. Seonu.

44:42.180 --> 44:43.431
Why would you…

44:43.890 --> 44:44.891
Thank you.

44:45.558 --> 44:47.809
I wanted to speak to you today

44:47.810 --> 44:50.229
as Haran's grandmother,
not the head of the atelier.

44:51.189 --> 44:54.858
Thank you so much for letting me see Haran

44:54.859 --> 44:58.029
crying and laughing again.

44:59.488 --> 45:01.199
No, I…

45:01.949 --> 45:03.116
I didn't do anything…

45:03.117 --> 45:04.951
They say that if it's fate,

45:04.952 --> 45:07.412
you'll meet
no matter how far apart you are.

45:07.413 --> 45:08.830
You came all the way here.

45:08.831 --> 45:11.208
I don't think
you were meant to just work here.

45:12.627 --> 45:13.669
Thanks to you,

45:14.587 --> 45:16.172
I'll be able to leave in peace.

45:17.840 --> 45:19.300
Are you going somewhere?

45:20.301 --> 45:21.302
Well,

45:22.720 --> 45:26.348
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

45:26.349 --> 45:28.058
If you stay by Haran's side,

45:28.059 --> 45:31.061
I won't be that worried about her.

45:31.062 --> 45:32.772
Ah.

45:34.774 --> 45:37.985
But, Ms. Kim,

45:39.237 --> 45:41.948
I may not be as good for her

45:43.449 --> 45:47.078
as you believe.

45:54.710 --> 45:57.421
My heart is throbbing,

45:58.631 --> 46:00.341
and tears keep flowing.

46:01.092 --> 46:02.093
My heart

46:03.261 --> 46:04.929
hurts more than my foot.

46:06.055 --> 46:07.847
Do you think it's serious?

46:07.848 --> 46:11.393
Cut the drama and go to a bigger hospital.

46:11.394 --> 46:13.061
I can't treat that properly here.

46:13.062 --> 46:15.606
I'm sure it's just because
I trained hard these days.

46:16.148 --> 46:17.857
Just give me something for the bruise.

46:25.449 --> 46:26.866
Can you move aside?

46:26.867 --> 46:28.618
Huh? Oh…

46:38.796 --> 46:40.213
Can I help you with anything?

46:40.214 --> 46:42.675
Why did Yougyum come here?

46:43.259 --> 46:44.592
Is he hurt?

46:44.593 --> 46:45.885
That's personal information.

46:48.597 --> 46:51.392
Is she sick or something?

46:54.020 --> 46:56.314
She has to stay healthy.

47:02.903 --> 47:04.946
Mmm.

47:04.947 --> 47:06.740
Hey, you came back.

47:06.741 --> 47:11.120
I finished my first appointment,
so I'm here for the next one with you.

47:13.664 --> 47:16.333
Seriously, what are we doing here?

47:16.334 --> 47:17.335
You'll see.

47:18.419 --> 47:21.505
KIM SEON POTTERY EXHIBITION

47:22.256 --> 47:23.716
Pottery exhibition?

47:24.967 --> 47:26.176
No way.

47:26.177 --> 47:28.137
-  Oh. You're here.
- Grandma!

47:30.139 --> 47:32.932
Goodness.

47:32.933 --> 47:34.976
-  I missed you.
- I feel neglected lately.

47:34.977 --> 47:36.186
-  How are you?
- It's okay.

47:36.187 --> 47:37.188
Have you been well?

47:37.855 --> 47:40.065
You should have told me
we were seeing her.

47:40.066 --> 47:41.901
It's not my fault. She told me not to.

47:42.777 --> 47:44.736
If I'd known, I would've gotten flowers--

47:44.737 --> 47:46.946
That's why I told him to keep it secret.

47:46.947 --> 47:51.035
And why would I need flowers
when such a precious guest is here?

47:51.786 --> 47:52.995
Are you two dating?

47:53.704 --> 47:55.205
You little brat.

47:55.206 --> 47:57.832
You should've told me
you were going to the States.

47:57.833 --> 48:00.627
- I was worried when I couldn't reach you.
- I told you.

48:00.628 --> 48:03.338
- I suddenly had to go--
- Still, you should have told her.

48:03.339 --> 48:04.422
Right?

48:04.423 --> 48:06.216
Wow. You're teaming up on me?

48:06.217 --> 48:07.717
That's so mean. I'm leaving.

48:07.718 --> 48:10.720
Come and look around.
And get the cup you made last time.

48:10.721 --> 48:12.722
It looks so beautiful.

48:12.723 --> 48:15.975
Really? I'm so excited.

48:15.976 --> 48:17.894
My hands look pretty, don't they?

48:17.895 --> 48:20.188
No one's coming for me?

48:20.189 --> 48:21.607
I want to be doted on, too!

48:35.579 --> 48:37.580
Oh. This one looks a bit different.

48:37.581 --> 48:41.209
The lines seem pretty rough,
but it's so cool.

48:41.210 --> 48:44.088
The lines are where I mended them.

48:44.672 --> 48:47.508
I put together the shattered pieces.

48:48.008 --> 48:49.926
You can put shattered pieces together?

48:49.927 --> 48:51.386
You know lacquer trees, right?

48:51.387 --> 48:53.681
The sap acts as a natural adhesive.

48:54.265 --> 48:57.684
Once I attach the pieces
and let them dry carefully…

48:57.685 --> 49:01.063
Then they become a new art piece.

49:02.898 --> 49:07.027
They shatter, get hurt, then heal,

49:07.653 --> 49:09.530
and in the process, they gain depth.

49:10.781 --> 49:12.992
It's similar to people, right?

49:16.454 --> 49:20.623
Oh… Would it be possible
to restore a broken plate?

49:20.624 --> 49:24.127
It's a dish my mom treasured,
but they don't sell it anymore.

49:24.128 --> 49:27.381
Bring it over sometime.
I'll do my best to restore it.

49:27.840 --> 49:29.591
Ms. Kim.

49:29.592 --> 49:31.969
You're here. Hang on.

49:32.553 --> 49:33.887
Look around.

49:36.557 --> 49:38.558
We shouldn't meet like this anymore.

49:38.559 --> 49:39.851
I just get lonely.

49:41.145 --> 49:44.522
Shouldn't you go and greet them?
They seem like her friends.

49:44.523 --> 49:46.441
Chan, come and say hi.

49:46.442 --> 49:47.901
Okay.

49:47.902 --> 49:49.403
I'll be back soon.

49:52.364 --> 49:55.533
Oh. The kid who visited during vacation?

49:55.534 --> 49:58.703
- Yes.
- You've gotten so handsome!

49:58.704 --> 50:01.456
Thank you.
I turned out pretty well, didn't I?

50:01.457 --> 50:04.125
Oh my. Look how cheeky he's gotten.

50:05.628 --> 50:07.420
You used to call him Chan.

50:07.421 --> 50:10.257
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

50:11.008 --> 50:12.384
Seonu Chan?

50:14.345 --> 50:15.471
Seonu…

50:16.305 --> 50:17.348
Chan.

50:21.894 --> 50:23.436
He's shameless, like me.

50:30.986 --> 50:33.071
Oh? There's no one here.

50:33.072 --> 50:34.697
Everyone went home.

50:34.698 --> 50:36.199
Is Hayeong not here?

50:36.200 --> 50:38.618
We were going to discuss
the new material today.

50:38.619 --> 50:41.412
She was feeble all day,
unlike her usual self,

50:41.413 --> 50:42.872
and went home early.

50:42.873 --> 50:44.374
Try calling her.

50:44.375 --> 50:45.376
Bye, then.

50:52.258 --> 50:54.008
Ms. Song.

50:54.009 --> 50:55.176
Hello?

50:55.177 --> 50:56.929
Are you a friend of hers?

50:58.138 --> 51:01.015
She's been drinking and sleeping nonstop.

51:01.016 --> 51:02.768
You should come and take her home.

51:15.781 --> 51:16.782
Ah.

51:17.408 --> 51:19.493
Good morning.

51:20.077 --> 51:21.661
When did I come to work, though?

51:21.662 --> 51:23.913
You got off work. This is a wine bar.

51:23.914 --> 51:25.498
I'll take you home.

51:25.499 --> 51:28.459
What? To where? Home?

51:28.460 --> 51:30.588
No, I can't.

51:31.589 --> 51:33.757
I can't face Hadam.

51:36.510 --> 51:40.097
I should have told her more
about Mom and Dad.

51:41.056 --> 51:43.392
I should have known how she felt.

51:44.435 --> 51:46.895
I should have known

51:47.688 --> 51:49.732
so no one would get hurt.

51:51.483 --> 51:55.236
Hadam was only six at the time.

51:55.237 --> 51:59.158
But she was in the car with Mom and Dad

51:59.950 --> 52:01.368
during…

52:02.244 --> 52:04.038
the accident…

52:17.635 --> 52:18.761
It's cold.

52:56.256 --> 52:59.677
It's just that you were crying…

53:00.177 --> 53:03.222
It's just drool.

53:03.931 --> 53:07.016
Let's go.

53:07.017 --> 53:08.894
All right.

53:11.063 --> 53:12.231
The GPS…

53:14.942 --> 53:16.484
Wait.

53:16.485 --> 53:17.777
Seongsu-dong?

53:25.536 --> 53:26.954
Was I mistaken?

53:28.080 --> 53:31.667
Did you go to Seongsu-dong last Thursday?

53:32.710 --> 53:34.336
You were with Grandma, right?

53:35.003 --> 53:37.088
- No. I'll start the car.
- Wait.

53:37.089 --> 53:39.006
I saw Grandma that day.

53:39.007 --> 53:41.218
I'm sure I saw her crying.

53:42.094 --> 53:44.011
She was crying?

53:44.012 --> 53:45.806
So you did go to Seongsu-dong, right?

53:47.808 --> 53:49.518
That woke me right up.

53:51.854 --> 53:52.980
Is something going on?

53:54.565 --> 53:56.023
What is it?

53:56.024 --> 53:58.360
I'm sorry, but just let this go for now.

53:59.695 --> 54:00.863
Please.

54:26.054 --> 54:28.431
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

54:33.479 --> 54:35.980
You can't stop looking at it.
Are you that impressed?

54:35.981 --> 54:37.774
Are you sure I really made this?

54:37.775 --> 54:39.776
Did you make it again
because it was a mess?

54:39.777 --> 54:41.612
Of course not.

54:42.321 --> 54:46.282
I'd love to have dinner with you,
but I'm meeting the people who helped me.

54:46.283 --> 54:49.660
I'll stay in Seoul for a few days,
so let's have a meal sometime.

54:49.661 --> 54:51.787
And bring your mother's dish then.

54:51.788 --> 54:53.164
All right.

54:53.165 --> 54:55.541
Her mother's dish? What do you mean?

54:55.542 --> 54:57.793
Why are you curious about everything?

54:57.794 --> 55:00.213
Grandma, don't do that in front of her.

55:00.214 --> 55:01.631
Your cheeks are so squishy.

55:05.260 --> 55:06.595
The weather's so nice.

55:07.179 --> 55:08.429
How about dinner--

55:08.430 --> 55:10.224
Sorry, but you should go home first.

55:10.933 --> 55:12.935
- I'll see you later.
- Where are you going?

55:13.477 --> 55:14.728
Ms. Song!

55:16.730 --> 55:19.565
Being overly polite
will hurt her feelings.

55:19.566 --> 55:22.194
But I should at least give her
some hand lotion.

55:23.862 --> 55:24.863
Huh?

55:29.618 --> 55:31.203
Oh? Did she leave?

55:32.704 --> 55:33.705
Hang on.

55:37.251 --> 55:39.126
- She's not here?
- Did she leave?

55:39.127 --> 55:40.545
We can come back…

55:42.923 --> 55:44.006
Hmm?

55:50.430 --> 55:52.181
Dad. Dad!

55:52.182 --> 55:54.226
What more do I have to do
to make you stop?

55:59.231 --> 56:00.648
Let's just go.

56:00.649 --> 56:03.026
- Wait, I…
-  Chan.

56:07.406 --> 56:09.408
You're back.

56:10.075 --> 56:13.119
He had business nearby

56:13.120 --> 56:16.790
and dropped by to greet me
when he saw the sign.

56:20.043 --> 56:21.169
It's been a while.

56:23.463 --> 56:26.424
There was
an international conference nearby.

56:26.425 --> 56:27.426
Your school…

56:28.093 --> 56:32.346
No, your former school
and some other schools--

56:32.347 --> 56:34.015
That's enough.

56:34.016 --> 56:35.434
I'm not even curious.

56:37.144 --> 56:38.895
- Let's go.
- How are you?

56:39.563 --> 56:41.648
How is your condition these days?

56:50.616 --> 56:51.742
Are you going somewhere?

56:55.245 --> 56:56.580
Why are you taking your passport?

56:57.414 --> 56:59.041
I don't want to stay in Korea.

56:59.625 --> 57:01.376
You made a good decision.

57:02.502 --> 57:06.339
You received enough treatment,
so you can return to school--

57:06.340 --> 57:07.758
I'm not…

57:08.759 --> 57:10.092
going back to school.

57:10.093 --> 57:11.386
I'm not studying anymore.

57:12.888 --> 57:15.057
What? You've already wasted so much time.

57:16.058 --> 57:19.478
Are you going to give up everything
just because of some accident?

57:19.978 --> 57:23.522
Stop acting like a child
and be reasonable.

57:23.523 --> 57:26.860
You should finish your master's
and move on to a PhD program…

57:27.486 --> 57:28.820
Do you not see me?

57:30.405 --> 57:34.201
I'm covered in burn scars,
and I can't hear on one side.

57:35.160 --> 57:37.579
- You call that "some accident"?
- It's in the past.

57:38.080 --> 57:39.705
Blaming it won't change anything.

57:39.706 --> 57:42.125
Enough with the pathetic self-pity!

57:46.880 --> 57:47.964
I get it now.

57:48.799 --> 57:52.301
This is why she left you.
It was because of you.

57:52.302 --> 57:54.054
She didn't just leave,

57:54.888 --> 57:56.389
you made her leave!

57:56.390 --> 57:58.224
I'll leave too.

57:58.225 --> 57:59.935
I'll live my own life,

58:00.477 --> 58:04.105
so just think
that your stupid, obedient son…

58:06.817 --> 58:07.943
died…

58:09.152 --> 58:11.071
in that explosion.

58:18.745 --> 58:20.079
Why are you acting like this?

58:20.080 --> 58:22.540
You never worried about me before.

58:25.210 --> 58:27.045
I saw you here earlier,

58:27.754 --> 58:31.550
so I left,
in case you'd feel uncomfortable.

58:33.009 --> 58:34.969
I didn't know you'd come back.

58:34.970 --> 58:36.054
You're right.

58:36.680 --> 58:38.347
I do feel uncomfortable.

58:38.348 --> 58:41.810
So if you ever see me anywhere again,

58:42.352 --> 58:43.436
don't even say hi.

58:43.437 --> 58:45.229
Chan, don't do this!

58:45.230 --> 58:47.815
Are you going to keep acting
like you're strangers?

58:47.816 --> 58:49.735
Since you've met… Hmm?

58:50.527 --> 58:52.195
Give her the flowers. I'm leaving.

58:53.989 --> 58:55.698
- Chan, let's talk--
- Stop!

59:11.757 --> 59:13.132
Chan! Don't. Stop.

59:13.133 --> 59:15.009
Let him go! Let go of him!

59:15.010 --> 59:16.177
Let him go.

59:16.178 --> 59:17.678
Don't do this!

59:17.679 --> 59:20.055
Chan, let him go!

59:20.056 --> 59:23.101
Go. Everyone, just go!

59:34.404 --> 59:36.239
Oh, dear. Let me see.

59:36.865 --> 59:38.158
Oh, no.

59:38.617 --> 59:39.700
I'm sorry.

59:39.701 --> 59:42.913
It's okay.
I didn't even notice. I'm really fine.

59:43.955 --> 59:46.875
Grandma, take care of her for me.

59:48.543 --> 59:50.003
Wait…

59:51.838 --> 59:53.131
He won't be able…

59:54.382 --> 59:56.176
to face you right now.

01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:16.696
Darn it…

01:00:29.334 --> 01:00:31.878
I'll be able to fix the shattered pottery,

01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:36.424
but I can't do anything
about their relationship.

01:00:37.425 --> 01:00:39.886
They've had a deep rift for a long time.

01:00:44.391 --> 01:00:46.058
You can take it.

01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:47.727
Sorry, hang on.

01:00:48.353 --> 01:00:49.688
Yes, Director.

01:00:50.689 --> 01:00:51.772
Yes.

01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:53.400
Of course.

01:01:02.242 --> 01:01:05.036
PROFESSOR SUNWOO SEOK

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:07.289
"Science University"?

01:01:09.624 --> 01:01:11.000
From the smell,

01:01:11.001 --> 01:01:13.419
it seemed like
diluted sodium hypochlorite solution.

01:01:13.420 --> 01:01:16.089
Because of the diffraction of sunlight,
the cloud particles…

01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:18.049
Petrichor.

01:01:18.675 --> 01:01:20.843
Your former school
and some other schools…

01:01:20.844 --> 01:01:22.511
I guess
you majored in that field.

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.555
It seems like
you majored in engineering.

01:01:24.556 --> 01:01:26.974
He never tells me
what he did before entering CalArts.

01:01:26.975 --> 01:01:28.685
I lived like a corpse.

01:01:42.115 --> 01:01:44.575
Laundry…

01:01:44.576 --> 01:01:45.827
Is there any laundry?

01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:02.092
What happened to the pen you always use?

01:02:02.093 --> 01:02:04.053
I lost it, and I never found it.

01:02:04.054 --> 01:02:05.555
I'll just use a new one now.

01:02:06.431 --> 01:02:07.766
It's nothing special.

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:09.976
Wait.

01:02:10.685 --> 01:02:12.729
Why is this pen here?

01:02:18.526 --> 01:02:20.070
Huh? Genius.

01:02:25.450 --> 01:02:26.952
Mr. Seonu.

01:02:27.827 --> 01:02:29.453
Oh? You're in here.

01:02:29.454 --> 01:02:31.705
Yes, I was collecting laundry.

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:34.166
But why did you come upstairs?

01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:36.210
Sorry, I came without asking.

01:02:36.211 --> 01:02:39.254
I just wanted to see Mr. Seonu.
I have something to give him.

01:02:39.255 --> 01:02:41.256
He hasn't come home yet.

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:42.841
Let's go. I'll make you coffee.

01:02:42.842 --> 01:02:44.427
- Okay.
- All right.

01:02:46.972 --> 01:02:48.264
What happened?

01:02:49.099 --> 01:02:50.516
Did you get hurt?

01:02:50.517 --> 01:02:52.309
It's just a small scratch.

01:02:52.310 --> 01:02:53.519
Let's go on a walk.

01:02:53.520 --> 01:02:55.479
Let's go on a walk.

01:02:55.480 --> 01:02:58.357
We didn't get to go
on a walk today.

01:02:58.358 --> 01:03:00.567
You can go. I don't need coffee.

01:03:00.568 --> 01:03:02.486
I'll wait here for Mr. Seonu.

01:03:02.487 --> 01:03:03.530
Are you sure?

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.490
Hey, Haran…

01:03:06.491 --> 01:03:08.952
About before…

01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:11.371
No, never mind.

01:03:11.955 --> 01:03:13.747
I'll be back soon.

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:14.958
Wait a moment.

01:03:15.500 --> 01:03:18.795
cafe SHIM

01:03:22.173 --> 01:03:23.508
Why isn't he coming?

01:03:28.638 --> 01:03:29.972
Oh?

01:03:29.973 --> 01:03:30.974
You're here.

01:03:40.150 --> 01:03:42.110
Where have you been this whole…

01:03:43.695 --> 01:03:46.155
Let's go inside. You look exhausted.

01:03:46.156 --> 01:03:47.490
I'm sorry.

01:03:48.074 --> 01:03:49.617
For leaving like that

01:03:50.493 --> 01:03:52.328
and for hurting you.

01:03:53.913 --> 01:03:55.123
It's okay.

01:03:56.124 --> 01:03:57.709
I'm totally fine.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:00.420
It's all my fault.

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:05.632
I was being selfish,
trying to stay by your side.

01:04:05.633 --> 01:04:06.718
What are you saying?

01:04:07.385 --> 01:04:09.763
Just make me some tea
instead of saying such nonsense.

01:04:25.779 --> 01:04:27.781
I've been thinking…

01:04:28.823 --> 01:04:33.744
I don't think it's a good idea
for us to be this close, so--

01:04:33.745 --> 01:04:34.996
You saw this, right?

01:04:35.622 --> 01:04:38.041
Wow. I was so surprised when I saw it.

01:04:39.209 --> 01:04:42.795
These lines are where she mended
the broken pieces.

01:04:42.796 --> 01:04:45.131
Don't they make this look more beautiful?

01:04:45.882 --> 01:04:48.510
It seems admirable, too.

01:04:49.094 --> 01:04:50.970
- Ms. Song.
- To me…

01:04:53.932 --> 01:04:55.350
you're these lines.

01:04:58.228 --> 01:04:59.521
Ms. Song!

01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:03.817
The first snow…

01:05:05.193 --> 01:05:06.360
Vapor trails…

01:05:06.361 --> 01:05:08.154
Wow, it's beautiful.

01:05:08.947 --> 01:05:10.448
Jamsugyo…

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:13.409
And a certain name…

01:05:14.327 --> 01:05:17.747
They were all sad memories,
so I thought I'd never get over them.

01:05:18.498 --> 01:05:21.417
But I found myself feeling okay,

01:05:22.418 --> 01:05:24.087
thanks to someone

01:05:25.088 --> 01:05:27.340
who covered them with good memories.

01:05:28.842 --> 01:05:32.387
But you say something like that
over a tiny scratch?

01:05:34.264 --> 01:05:36.432
It's a relief I met you here.

01:05:38.184 --> 01:05:40.395
Thanks to you, I found a way,

01:05:40.979 --> 01:05:44.440
so this time, why don't you try it…

01:05:46.401 --> 01:05:47.443
with your father?

01:05:50.321 --> 01:05:51.739
That's impossible.

01:05:54.784 --> 01:05:56.578
You remember when we first met, right?

01:05:57.412 --> 01:06:00.248
I was cold and avoided you.

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:03.585
I thought it was impossible too.

01:06:04.169 --> 01:06:08.339
But I guess there's no such thing
as never in a relationship.

01:06:09.090 --> 01:06:11.801
Aren't I a good example of that?

01:06:17.473 --> 01:06:19.434
I picked this up at the exhibit.

01:06:21.102 --> 01:06:23.103
He must wear this all the time.

01:06:23.104 --> 01:06:24.689
It's in the photo as well.

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:30.319
I've never seen it before.

01:06:30.320 --> 01:06:31.529
Really?

01:06:32.405 --> 01:06:36.075
The drawing here looks similar
to the one I saw at your grandma's place.

01:06:42.665 --> 01:06:46.502
He must have kept wearing it
even when it was broken.

01:06:48.588 --> 01:06:50.423
I bought that for him a long time ago

01:06:51.549 --> 01:06:53.218
at a stationary store

01:06:54.427 --> 01:06:55.887
for Parents' Day.

01:06:56.846 --> 01:06:58.139
Maybe…

01:06:58.973 --> 01:07:01.142
he wanted to mend things.

01:07:01.726 --> 01:07:04.354
He's been wearing this broken watch
the whole time.

01:07:16.783 --> 01:07:18.743
I should give you some time alone.

01:07:23.665 --> 01:07:24.832
Thank you.

01:07:33.633 --> 01:07:38.429
I have a habit
of hugging people I want to comfort.

01:07:39.639 --> 01:07:41.224
That's my thing.

01:07:42.725 --> 01:07:44.060
Why do you keep copying me?

01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:50.233
I wish we'd met earlier.

01:07:51.109 --> 01:07:54.195
Then we could've gotten close faster,
and I would've been nicer first.

01:07:55.655 --> 01:07:58.240
I would have at least given you a hug

01:07:58.241 --> 01:08:01.119
when you were scared to open your eyes.

01:08:10.628 --> 01:08:14.006
You saved me as well.

01:08:21.306 --> 01:08:24.642
You already did that for me.

01:08:41.284 --> 01:08:46.873
Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

01:08:47.665 --> 01:08:52.252
The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

01:08:52.253 --> 01:08:54.087
Her boyfriend died back then.

01:08:54.088 --> 01:08:56.673
He went to study in Boston,
but he suddenly died.

01:09:01.929 --> 01:09:05.933
"Newbury Street, Boston?"

01:09:15.485 --> 01:09:17.362
I've only
received things from you.

01:09:21.366 --> 01:09:23.284
I should be really nice to you
from now on.

01:09:26.996 --> 01:09:28.039
Then…

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:32.710
I might end up liking you even more.

01:09:33.336 --> 01:09:34.879
It's okay…

01:09:36.214 --> 01:09:37.340
if you like me more.

01:09:39.509 --> 01:09:40.718
If I like you more…

01:09:44.597 --> 01:09:46.057
I might get more greedy.

01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:50.603
It's okay

01:09:51.854 --> 01:09:53.314
if you get more greedy.

01:10:46.033 --> 01:10:48.034
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:11:12.059 --> 01:11:16.188
Why do you keep saying
it's greedy to like me?

01:11:16.189 --> 01:11:18.648
-  You mean it, right?
-  Yes.

01:11:18.649 --> 01:11:22.736
How about letting time
with your dad start moving again?

01:11:22.737 --> 01:11:24.654
The past is the past,

01:11:24.655 --> 01:11:28.116
and what matters is the time you have now.

01:11:28.117 --> 01:11:30.660
There's nothing wrong with her, right?

01:11:30.661 --> 01:11:34.039
What on earth is happening to you?

01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:37.000
Seonu Chan found this pen for you.

01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:39.461
And this is a lucky charm.

01:11:39.462 --> 01:11:42.298
No way. What is this?

01:11:56.270 --> 01:11:57.354
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:11:57.355 --> 01:11:58.356
Translated by Juyoung Park
